WEBVTT

00:00:09.615 --> 00:00:14.245
Hatenkou Yugi

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.556
Tabidachi wa sone totsuzen

00:00:18.557 --> 00:00:22.027
Guzen no yona hitsuzen

00:00:22.027 --> 00:00:27.829
Mawari dashita unmei ga kishimu

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:32.268
Totsuzen no ame ni sozen

00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:35.706
Furarete zubunure bozen

00:00:35.707 --> 00:00:41.805
Warai tobase michi wa hirakareru

00:00:42.447 --> 00:00:45.616
Muimi na koto ni kakusareteru

00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:49.187
Ichiban daiji na mono wa nani

00:00:49.187 --> 00:00:57.094
Kitto kiseki wa okosu mono waratte

00:00:57.763 --> 00:01:00.596
My Heartbreaking Romance

00:01:00.799 --> 00:01:04.836
Hajikeyo omou mama ni

00:01:04.836 --> 00:01:10.138
Omoshiro yukai sore ga kihon

00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:14.171
Kimi no Heartrending Sorrow

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:18.416
Ima wa mada furenai yo

00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:24.879
Mazu wa koko kara hajimeyo

00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:29.992
Am | ever

00:01:32.431 --> 00:01:34.626
What a romantic view.

00:01:34.967 --> 00:01:37.265
Yes, it’s truly breathtaking.

00:01:38.403 --> 00:01:40.564
The shining moon that coldly lights up the world.

00:01:40.939 --> 00:01:43.874
The snowy hills reflecting the pale blue light.

00:01:44.276 --> 00:01:47.473
This is the perfect moment...
to leave as many footprints as | want!

00:01:48.513 --> 00:01:50.037
You’re gonna fall, Rahzel-chan.

00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:52.150
See?

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:53.447
Uh-oh.

00:01:56.955 --> 00:01:59.857
Man, you’re completely covered with snow.

00:01:59.858 --> 00:02:03.191
You're acting like a silly puppy.

00:02:04.062 --> 00:02:07.054
Besides, what was with that poetic talk anyway?

00:02:07.899 --> 00:02:09.924
That’s your problem, Al-kiddo.

00:02:10.202 --> 00:02:12.193
You don’t appreciate such elegance.

00:02:12.471 --> 00:02:16.202
On this moonlit night,
Alzeid does not assimilate its elegance.

00:02:20.245 --> 00:02:26.980
The white hair reveals his poor upbringing,
as | remember the moon over Mt. Mikasa.

00:02:31.323 --> 00:02:33.723
That is a poem about yearning for home!

00:02:41.466 --> 00:02:42.433
An avalanche’?!

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:44.669
No way! | didn’t see any sign of it!

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:45.227
Run!

00:02:46.905 --> 00:02:50.136
Hey, why don’t we escape
into the sky using magic?

00:02:50.308 --> 00:02:51.172
Good idea!

00:02:51.309 --> 00:02:53.834
Huh? Wait! You’re ditching me?

00:02:54.212 --> 00:02:57.443
At a time like this, all you need
is the ability to think calmly.

00:02:57.883 --> 00:03:00.545
Look how easily we escaped from the crisis.

00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:04.489
Yeah, we must be thankful to the man
who died saving our lives.

00:03:04.489 --> 00:03:06.719
Don’t speak of me in the past tense!

00:03:07.626 --> 00:03:08.957
Good luck, Heat-tan!

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:12.319
Rahzel!

00:03:13.198 --> 00:03:14.130
Rahzel-chan!

00:03:18.203 --> 00:03:22.139
haAen
the Flower Blooms

00:03:23.041 --> 00:03:24.133
You’ve never seen the sky?

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:28.109
| know of it, so it’s not a problem for me.

00:03:29.881 --> 00:03:33.044
It’s the same blue as your eyes.

00:03:43.028 --> 00:03:45.963
They are the same! The same color as mine!

00:03:52.104 --> 00:03:54.732
Just like me, you have white and red!

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:58.598
Y-yeah, I’m an albino...

00:04:04.249 --> 00:04:06.410
Hey, Al-kiddo, are you awake?

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:09.082
Huh?

00:04:10.555 --> 00:04:11.579
Your illegitimate child?

00:04:11.757 --> 00:04:13.884
You're right. They have
the exact same coloring.

00:04:14.192 --> 00:04:15.386
You guys are morons.

00:04:16.762 --> 00:04:17.990
Where are we?

00:04:18.563 --> 00:04:21.054
| thought we were caught up in the avalanche.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.469
Well, | thought so, too...

00:04:25.036 --> 00:04:25.934
Little Lady...

00:04:27.839 --> 00:04:28.999
Are you from that village?

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:34.078
Um, what’s your name?

00:04:34.312 --> 00:04:36.246
Ludovika! Ludovika!

00:04:37.682 --> 00:04:39.950
Ludovika! Ludovika!

00:04:39.951 --> 00:04:41.519
So your name is Ludovika?

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:42.988
Looks like someone’s here to take you home...

00:04:42.988 --> 00:04:43.477
Huh?!

00:04:45.123 --> 00:04:47.853
Wh-wh-what’s going on?

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.624
My apologies.

00:04:57.235 --> 00:05:00.295
They mistakenly thought
you were trying to harm Ludovika.

00:05:00.872 --> 00:05:03.568
How long are you going
to stay like that, Ludovika?

00:05:03.708 --> 00:05:07.644
Basically, it was your fault
for sneaking out of the village again.

00:05:08.446 --> 00:05:10.038
You should apologize properly.

00:05:12.617 --> 00:05:17.117
As you can see, for this girl
who lacks melanin pigment in her skin and eyes,

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:20.387
the sunlight is a great enemy.

00:05:20.592 --> 00:05:25.894
We don’t allow her to go outside during the day,
of course, or even let her open the curtains.

00:05:26.531 --> 00:05:34.097
Because of that, she often sneaks out of
the village hoping to see the daylight sky.

00:05:35.407 --> 00:05:39.366
Alzeid-san, | see you have
the same physical traits.

00:05:39.644 --> 00:05:41.407
How can you stay outside without a problem?

00:05:43.248 --> 00:05:44.647
What do you want to know?

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:49.381
How I'm able to go out in the sun like anyone else?

00:05:49.955 --> 00:05:55.791
If she wishes, you could simply
give her sunscreen and sunglasses.

00:05:57.696 --> 00:06:01.496
Except for her poor vision
and extreme sensitivity to UV rays,

00:06:01.867 --> 00:06:03.357
she isn’t any different from other people.

00:06:03.802 --> 00:06:09.832
She is just a normal child whose intelligence
and physical abilities are as high as others.

00:06:10.809 --> 00:06:13.835
That may be true in the outside world.

00:06:14.179 --> 00:06:22.052
However, for us to have the sun taken away
is no less than being deprived of our right to live.

00:06:22.487 --> 00:06:27.390
Ludovika was born with this condition,
and yet she still seeks sunlight.

00:06:27.893 --> 00:06:31.522
| suppose that’s the instinct we cannot ignore.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:33.598
Sir, you shouldn't be...

00:06:38.036 --> 00:06:39.637
That’s enough talking, | suppose.

00:06:39.638 --> 00:06:42.505
Well, we have prepared a room
for you for tonight.

00:06:42.707 --> 00:06:44.868
Please make yourselves at home.

00:06:45.677 --> 00:06:47.736
Now, come with us, Ludovika.

00:06:49.547 --> 00:06:51.447
For crying out loud.

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:52.776
| apologize.

00:06:52.951 --> 00:06:55.613
Make sure to go to bed before it gets too late.

00:06:57.389 --> 00:07:01.985
Alzeid, what was that eyesight thing about?
Are you all right?

00:07:02.594 --> 00:07:07.258
Yeah. Although, | have trouble
finding you sometimes.

00:07:07.699 --> 00:07:10.998
Since you’re a shrimp,
you don’t always come into our sight.

00:07:11.436 --> 00:07:13.233
| have a good idea.

00:07:13.738 --> 00:07:17.572
Why don’t | make you guys one head shorter?

00:07:18.376 --> 00:07:20.970
No worries. You actually have advantages.

00:07:21.246 --> 00:07:25.342
Like, you can try some acrobatic positions
when there’s a big height difference...

00:07:28.753 --> 00:07:29.720
Owl Ow!

00:07:29.721 --> 00:07:30.755
You cut me!
Those morons...

00:07:30.755 --> 00:07:31.813
No | didn't!
Those morons...

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:35.917
| thought nobody
with this coloring could go outside.

00:07:36.428 --> 00:07:38.919
What’s the sky like when it’s bright?

00:07:39.331 --> 00:07:41.799
It’s blue... but you might not get it, huh?

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.267
Let’s see...

00:07:43.868 --> 00:07:45.927
Look at her eyes. That’s the same color.

00:07:46.404 --> 00:07:48.139
Now, what shall | start with?

00:07:48.139 --> 00:07:49.731
Your neck or knees?

00:07:49.874 --> 00:07:53.944
Even if it’s by your request,
I’m not really into that hardcore stuff...

00:07:53.945 --> 00:07:55.572
Don’t waste your breath.

00:07:55.981 --> 00:07:58.711
Are you done with your prayers yet?

00:07:58.950 --> 00:07:59.678
Ow!

00:08:03.788 --> 00:08:05.153
What an idiot.

00:08:05.623 --> 00:08:06.783
Alzeid-san...

00:08:07.058 --> 00:08:09.219
is the color of the sky always like that?

00:08:09.761 --> 00:08:12.130
Not always, but for the most part.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.223
Wow! It’s so beautiful!

00:08:17.502 --> 00:08:20.096
Yeah, it is.

00:08:20.872 --> 00:08:23.841
You’ve never seen the sky?

00:08:24.476 --> 00:08:28.640
So what? I’m not troubled by it.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:30.081
You don’t mean that.

00:08:30.081 --> 00:08:33.847
You’re wrong. | know of it,
so it’s not a problem.

00:08:34.552 --> 00:08:36.452
It’s the same color as those eyes of yours.

00:08:38.456 --> 00:08:40.822
You’re more romantic than | thought.

00:08:41.326 --> 00:08:42.994
5-stop laughing!

00:08:42.994 --> 00:08:45.827
Wanna go see it with me?

00:08:46.598 --> 00:08:49.795
No way... My father would never allow that.

00:08:50.502 --> 00:08:53.027
| know. So we'll do it quietly.

00:08:53.304 --> 00:08:54.999
Quietly, in secret.

00:08:56.741 --> 00:08:57.503
What?

00:08:57.675 --> 00:08:59.700
We can quietly take her out in secret.

00:08:59.944 --> 00:09:03.277
But | guess that’s not the point here.

00:09:04.115 --> 00:09:04.672
Right.

00:09:11.723 --> 00:09:17.491
Although they’re both blue, the colors of the sky
and my eyes are totally different.

00:09:18.129 --> 00:09:20.996
| wish | could show her the true color of the sky.

00:09:23.968 --> 00:09:24.992
Something wrong?

00:09:25.804 --> 00:09:27.465
No, | thought | heard something.

00:09:27.806 --> 00:09:31.003
By the way, what are you up to?

00:09:31.943 --> 00:09:35.174
Tell us the truth.
You can’t stand the cold, right?

00:09:35.513 --> 00:09:38.414
If you force yourself
to act like a hyperactive character,

00:09:38.683 --> 00:09:41.413
this is when your true colors show.

00:09:41.653 --> 00:09:43.553
Y-you got it all wrong!

00:09:43.721 --> 00:09:47.020
I’m not heating this up just for myself!

00:09:47.659 --> 00:09:48.523
He’s a tsundere?

00:09:49.227 --> 00:09:54.859
It’s not just the chill | feel...
don’t you feel someone staring at you?

00:09:55.667 --> 00:09:59.262
Ever since we arrived in this village,
it feels like someone’s been watching us...

00:09:59.571 --> 00:10:02.774
and the hair on the back of my neck
is standing straight up.

00:10:02.774 --> 00:10:03.741
Staring?

00:10:04.042 --> 00:10:07.842
Yup, and it’s not just one person,
but tons of them.

00:10:08.446 --> 00:10:09.913
The weird thing is...

00:10:10.381 --> 00:10:16.445
| just checked the map,
and there shouldn't be any village around here.

00:10:16.821 --> 00:10:20.484
That might be true in the outside world, but...

00:10:20.692 --> 00:10:21.386
Here.

00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:23.290
Sure.

00:10:26.264 --> 00:10:27.822
It’s too hot, and too bitter.

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:31.892
| didn’t make coffee just for you!

00:10:32.103 --> 00:10:34.037
Stop acting like that already.

00:10:34.639 --> 00:10:35.663
Where are you going?

00:10:36.274 --> 00:10:37.764
| don’t need coffee anymore.

00:10:37.976 --> 00:10:39.705
ll go brush my teeth and go to bed.

00:10:42.981 --> 00:10:44.048
What a relief...

00:10:44.048 --> 00:10:44.980
Thank goodness...

00:10:45.316 --> 00:10:47.580
Ludovika will be saved now.

00:10:48.419 --> 00:10:52.378
Without them, Ludovika wouldn't
have survived until next spring.

00:10:52.924 --> 00:10:55.085
The more fertilizer the better.

00:10:55.293 --> 00:10:59.627
Yeah, but making Ludovika sad
is the last thing | want to do.

00:11:00.064 --> 00:11:01.691
Don’t be naive.

00:11:01.933 --> 00:11:02.922
Say no more.

00:11:03.168 --> 00:11:05.436
What we must protect is our child.

00:11:05.436 --> 00:11:07.028
Our future depends on her.

00:11:07.672 --> 00:11:09.503
Yes, indeed.

00:11:10.842 --> 00:11:13.743
| suppose we have no choice but to let them die.

00:11:35.266 --> 00:11:38.667
Hey, you sure we didn’t have to
say goodbye to Ludovika?

00:11:38.903 --> 00:11:40.734
Shut up and walk, without arguing.

00:11:41.105 --> 00:11:43.699
A Senryu needs one more phrase, Al-kiddo.

00:11:44.008 --> 00:11:45.498
Just shut up already.

00:11:46.044 --> 00:11:48.706
So you heard about dying or fertilizer?

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:51.105
Are you sure you weren’t dreaming?

00:11:51.583 --> 00:11:55.815
| mean, you tend to sleepwalk,
Alzeid, quite often.

00:11:56.321 --> 00:11:58.812
It’s not quite often. Only once in a blue moon.

00:11:59.424 --> 00:12:03.417
Well, it doesn’t matter.
| didn’t want to stay there too long anyway.

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:10.761
| mean, Baroqueheat mentioned someone staring.

00:12:11.236 --> 00:12:13.534
Exactly. Even now...

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:16.438
What was that?

00:12:16.708 --> 00:12:18.175
The forest just moved.

00:12:20.545 --> 00:12:22.240
No way.

00:12:23.181 --> 00:12:24.273
“The forest just moved.”

00:12:24.482 --> 00:12:25.449
That’s funny.

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:26.678
You little...

00:12:26.818 --> 00:12:30.777
Still, one thing we know for sure
is that we’re going around in circles.

00:12:33.558 --> 00:12:34.388
It’s you...

00:12:37.462 --> 00:12:40.158
ll guide you out of the forest.

00:12:41.099 --> 00:12:41.861
They’re gone!

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.691
They got away. Ludovika must’ve gone with them!

00:12:47.238 --> 00:12:49.206
Now, what should we do?

00:12:49.641 --> 00:12:52.276
We must act now. It'll be dawn soon.

00:12:52.277 --> 00:12:53.938
Then, it’ll be too late.

00:12:54.345 --> 00:12:57.974
We must take care of it while our comrades
on the edge of the woods buy us time.

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:00.949
We have no choice.

00:13:03.121 --> 00:13:04.315
They noticed, huh?

00:13:06.858 --> 00:13:11.090
Thank you, but we’re fine from here.

00:13:11.396 --> 00:13:13.023
Um, but...

00:13:13.731 --> 00:13:15.130
Do you want to wait for the dawn?

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:16.758
Y-yes!

00:13:18.136 --> 00:13:22.630
To reduce the risk of skin cancer,
you need to avoid the sun.

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:25.773
As a result, your bones and teeth
tend to become brittle.

00:13:26.711 --> 00:13:28.508
In addition to your poor vision,

00:13:28.746 --> 00:13:33.246
lacking the pigmentation in the eye that blocks off
the excess light causes even poorer vision.

00:13:34.218 --> 00:13:35.276
Alzeid?

00:13:36.187 --> 00:13:42.023
This isn’t something you can cure with surgery
or improve your immunity to over time.

00:13:42.927 --> 00:13:46.522
You're destined to live with this illness for life.

00:13:46.798 --> 00:13:47.730
Do you understand?

00:13:47.932 --> 00:13:48.762
Yes.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:53.500
That said, it doesn’t mean there’s no way
you can have a normal life.

00:13:54.205 --> 00:13:57.732
As a congenital disorder,
this is considered a mild case.

00:13:58.776 --> 00:14:04.442
Even with that in mind, | must say that the way
they treat you is overly protective.

00:14:05.049 --> 00:14:06.283
You understand that, too, right?

00:14:06.284 --> 00:14:06.773
Yes.

00:14:07.485 --> 00:14:12.479
But even so, your behavior
isn’t something to be praised.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:16.892
For your desire to see the blue sky,
do you realize how much trouble you’ve caused?

00:14:17.628 --> 00:14:22.691
Your act of being here is a betrayal
of all the people who love and protect you.

00:14:22.867 --> 00:14:24.528
Do you understand that?

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:26.829
Yes.

00:14:27.672 --> 00:14:29.731
Then, suit yourself.

00:14:30.007 --> 00:14:31.201
Alzeid!

00:14:31.642 --> 00:14:34.110
Everyone chooses their own path.

00:14:34.512 --> 00:14:35.813
Isn’t that your thing?

00:14:35.813 --> 00:14:36.575
Huh?

00:14:37.615 --> 00:14:39.083
Yeah, | guess.

00:14:39.083 --> 00:14:41.449
Well, I'll choose mine then.

00:14:42.153 --> 00:14:45.782
We shall now perform a ritual
for blocking the sun.

00:14:47.759 --> 00:14:52.259
Beyond this point is a girls’ private space,
so you aren’t allowed to cross.

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:55.863
Also, whoever has sunglasses,
hand them to me.

00:14:56.234 --> 00:15:02.002
And so, this is how Rahzel-chan
ended up taking part in the kidnapping.

00:15:02.673 --> 00:15:04.732
Where did my sunglasses go?

00:15:05.009 --> 00:15:07.034
Could she be any more meddlesome?

00:15:09.046 --> 00:15:14.484
As a kid, | didn’t know the outside world,
let alone the color of the sky.

00:15:14.952 --> 00:15:20.254
There was a meddilesome woman
who encouraged me to see the outside.

00:15:21.459 --> 00:15:24.622
| didn’t even know her name.
She was just a foolish woman.

00:15:25.830 --> 00:15:29.231
And that was the first time
| saw the color of the sky.

00:15:34.005 --> 00:15:37.575
Just to be sure, let’s put some sunscreen
under your clothes, too.

00:15:37.575 --> 00:15:39.372
It might be cold, but be patient, okay?

00:15:40.111 --> 00:15:41.203
He said | was normal.

00:15:42.413 --> 00:15:46.372
Alzeid-san said that | was normal.

00:15:46.851 --> 00:15:50.184
But this isn’t normal, is it?

00:15:50.888 --> 00:15:55.985
I’m causing this much trouble
just to go outside...

00:15:56.594 --> 00:15:59.188
He’s pretty tall.

00:16:00.998 --> 00:16:04.331
He has long legs and walks fast.

00:16:04.735 --> 00:16:08.933
He tells me not to push myself too hard,
and yet he totally ignores my pace.

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:13.936
Once | reach the point where | collapse,
he finally turns around and stops.

00:16:14.345 --> 00:16:17.940
But the moment | get up, he takes off again.

00:16:18.716 --> 00:16:20.650
Talk about being self-centered.

00:16:21.886 --> 00:16:28.917
But he lets me be normal by doing that,
and gives me a hand when I’m absolutely helpless.

00:16:29.694 --> 00:16:34.131
If | have someone like that, my disadvantage
becomes an advantage in my book.

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:38.698
But lately, | don’t give up so easily.

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:40.301
I've built up my physical strength now.

00:16:40.705 --> 00:16:45.267
Do you think... my disadvantage
will go away, too?

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:49.268
Of course. It’s not going to be easy...

00:16:49.881 --> 00:16:57.219
but as long as you keep fighting for it,
and find someone who fights for you, you can do it!

00:17:05.296 --> 00:17:06.730
The heroine is in trouble!

00:17:06.731 --> 00:17:08.358
Was that a scream?

00:17:09.166 --> 00:17:10.224
Well, whatever.

00:17:14.639 --> 00:17:15.606
What the hell is that?

00:17:15.806 --> 00:17:16.830
I don’t know!

00:17:17.174 --> 00:17:18.300
Isn’t that kinda suggestive?

00:17:18.442 --> 00:17:19.743
Go get ‘em, tentacle!

00:17:19.744 --> 00:17:21.143
Are you on their side?

00:17:21.312 --> 00:17:22.677
Strip her skirt off!

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:23.912
Where's the kid?

00:17:24.248 --> 00:17:25.180
Over there.

00:17:28.019 --> 00:17:30.579
Stop! Everyone, please stop!

00:17:35.126 --> 00:17:38.195
| think we'll complete the game
if we defeat the final boss.

00:17:38.195 --> 00:17:40.686
Isn’t that old man pulling the magic strings?

00:17:40.998 --> 00:17:43.193
You sure this is magic?

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:50.740
What's this?

00:17:50.741 --> 00:17:54.978
It’s hard to describe,
but it feels like every branch has its own will.

00:17:54.979 --> 00:17:58.972
It’s neither hostility nor hatred,
but something more like a desperate prayer...

00:17:59.383 --> 00:18:00.816
Damn, it’s endless!

00:18:02.286 --> 00:18:04.151
Message from the commander!

00:18:04.422 --> 00:18:06.991
The target has moved to two o'clock!

00:18:06.991 --> 00:18:08.720
You better fight, too!

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:10.825
For us...

00:18:11.195 --> 00:18:14.631
this is the only way.

00:18:14.899 --> 00:18:17.026
Due to the rapid climate change,

00:18:17.268 --> 00:18:21.102
the valley is always covered with snow,
and we seldom have sunshine.

00:18:21.405 --> 00:18:24.169
We can only grow old and wait for death.

00:18:24.976 --> 00:18:29.174
What’s wrong with wanting to protect
the new life we’re blessed with in this situation?

00:18:29.347 --> 00:18:33.681
For our daughter who was born
an albino, we need fertilizer.

00:18:33.951 --> 00:18:37.079
What’s wrong with seeking
a human life to save her?

00:18:42.927 --> 00:18:47.455
Don’t drag me... into your selfish conspiracy!

00:18:54.572 --> 00:18:55.539
Alzeid!

00:18:55.773 --> 00:18:57.866
Looks like something
flipped his switch somehow.

00:19:00.044 --> 00:19:02.239
Shoot, he’s totally losing control.

00:19:28.506 --> 00:19:29.473
Ludovika...

00:19:31.642 --> 00:19:33.837
Dammit, don’t talk. Are you hurt?

00:19:34.712 --> 00:19:37.180
l-| can see the sky...

00:19:37.648 --> 00:19:40.845
The blue that you told me about, Alzeid-san...

00:20:03.607 --> 00:20:09.011
So beautiful. That’s the color
I’ve been dreaming of for so long.

00:20:10.581 --> 00:20:11.639
I’m so happy.

00:20:15.619 --> 00:20:20.886
Pure white petals, fluttering down like snow...

00:20:21.358 --> 00:20:23.918
Fertilizer, for saving Ludovika.

00:20:24.528 --> 00:20:26.928
Right, now | get it.

00:20:27.565 --> 00:20:28.532
Huh? What just happened?

00:20:28.699 --> 00:20:30.894
Where did those tentacles go?

00:20:32.703 --> 00:20:34.102
Photosynthesis.

00:20:35.473 --> 00:20:41.844
Since albino plants lack the chlorophyll
to have photosynthesis, it’s hard for them to grow.

00:20:42.613 --> 00:20:47.243
So if there was a way to supplement them
with another source of nutrition...

00:20:48.419 --> 00:20:51.684
When my father was killed
and that woman disappeared,

00:20:51.956 --> 00:20:54.186
| saw the sky for the very first time.

00:20:54.959 --> 00:20:58.827
It was so bright that it made me feel like
it was laughing at my own insignificant imagination.

00:21:01.732 --> 00:21:05.099
Still, your eyes were far more...

00:21:06.871 --> 00:21:07.671
What is it?

00:21:07.671 --> 00:21:10.435
Hey, look at that.

00:21:13.844 --> 00:21:14.674
Alzeid?

00:21:15.312 --> 00:21:16.609
Don’t be poky.

00:21:17.715 --> 00:21:18.739
Let’s get going.

00:21:20.417 --> 00:21:24.917
Once the snow melts and the sun shines,
a flower or two will bloom in the spring.

00:21:25.956 --> 00:21:27.958
Wow, how elegant.

00:21:27.958 --> 00:21:29.892
You're a poet, Alzeid.

00:21:43.674 --> 00:21:47.344
Tonari no heya kara

00:21:47.344 --> 00:21:50.973
Waraigoe ga suru

00:21:51.148 --> 00:21:58.350
Ussura mezameru asa ga konna ni Itoshii

00:21:58.722 --> 00:22:05.958
Dokoka de yumemita ichimai no e ni wa

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:13.534
Mou anata no isu wo kakitashita bakari da yo

00:22:13.704 --> 00:22:18.204
Kanashii monogatari ga ima

00:22:20.644 --> 00:22:29.348
Curtain no mukogawa machibuse shite itemo

00:22:31.355 --> 00:22:38.591
Ashita ni wa mishiranu hito no yoni nattemo

00:22:38.863 --> 00:22:45.996
Anata ga koko ni iru tashika na kiseki wo shinjite

00:22:46.303 --> 00:22:53.641
Sashidasareta te ni wa wakare no yokan mo naku

00:22:53.978 --> 00:23:01.714
Tada dakishimetakute ima ruisen ga yurunda
